.TH CHATGPT-WEB 1 "2026-11-24" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chatgpt-web \- local website companion for terminal Emacs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chatgpt-web
.RI [ options ] " command"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls the ChatGPT website using a dedicated Chromium profile and the local
DevTools pipe. Runs without an X server in normal operation. Requires no API key.
Website compatibility and terminal authentication are experimental.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B auth
Interact with the website's authentication forms in a terminal.
.TP
.B bridge
Serve JSON-line requests on stdin and send events and results on stdout.
.TP
.B doctor [--probe]
Report dependencies; optionally test browser startup and HTTPS website loading.
.TP
.B apply-patch FILE --directory DIR [--strip N] [--check]
Check, then apply an explicitly selected patch using git apply.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --profile DIR
Use a dedicated persistent Chromium profile.
.TP
.B --browser FILE
Select the Chromium executable.
.TP
.B --selectors FILE
Load JSON selector overrides.
.TP
.B --headed
Use a visible browser for optional interactive authentication. Requires display.
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Maximum response-following time; default 600.
.SH EMACS
Start with M-x chatgpt-web. Use M-x chatgpt-web-login for authentication.
See /usr/share/doc/emacs-chatgpt-web/README.fr.md for controls and limitations.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/chatgpt-web/profile
Dedicated private browser profile, unless XDG_DATA_HOME or --profile changes it.
.SH SECURITY
Passwords are accepted interactively or through private stdin, never as command
line arguments. Browser session cookies persist. Scripts run only after an
explicit user command and have the user's normal permissions.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Some MFA, SSO, passkey or visual checks require a browser interaction that this
text interface cannot provide. No protective measures or rate limits are bypassed.
